-# TCN-POWER-CURVE
+# TCN Power Curve
+
 > **Category:** SCADA Anomaly Detection  
+> **Platform adapter:** `m03-tcn-power-curve`  
+> **Status:** integrated  
+> **Collection position:** model **21** of 25 (alphabetical)
+
+<!-- Generated from deployment/models.catalog.json - edit the catalog, not this file. -->
+
+A causal temporal convolutional network that tracks the aerodynamic power curve and flags residual drift away from it. It is the collection's fastest way to answer the oldest question in wind O&M: is this turbine producing what its own history says it should at this wind speed?
+
+## How this page fits the collection
+
+The WT-PM collection numbers its 25 repositories **alphabetically 01-25** - that is the number on this page - and gives each one a **task-based adapter id** (`m03-tcn-power-curve`) used by the platform registry, the `wt-pm` CLI and the fusion engine. Both are printed on every page so the ecosystem graph and the registry can be read against each other.
+
+- Repository: <https://github.com/rajaram-2005/wt-pm-tcn-power-curve>
+- Landing page: <https://rajaram-2005.github.io/wt-pm-tcn-power-curve/>
+- Ecosystem graph: <https://rajaram-2005.github.io/wt-pm-lstm-scada-anomaly/ecosystem.html>
+- Platform architecture: <https://github.com/rajaram-2005/wt-pm-lstm-scada-anomaly/blob/main/ARCHITECTURE.md>
+- Per-model table: <https://github.com/rajaram-2005/wt-pm-lstm-scada-anomaly/blob/main/platform/docs/MODELS.md>
+
+## Model
+
+- `TemporalConvNet in model.py`
+- `Platform adapter trains it against the power channel`
+
+| Block | Detail |
+|---|---|
+| Dilated causal convolutions | Kernel size k over L layers with exponentially growing dilation; the receptive field grows as (k-1) * 2^L |
+| Residual blocks | Each block adds its input back, which keeps deep stacks trainable |
+| Head | Power forecast for the next step; residual against measured power is the anomaly score |
+
+## Advanced concepts
+
+The ideas this model actually leans on - stated with their failure modes, not as marketing.
+
+### Receptive field by dilation
+
+Two conv layers with kernel 3 see 5 samples; with dilation 1, 2, 4 the same two layers see 15. Causal TCNs buy long memory with convolution parallelism instead of recurrence's sequential dependency.
+
+### Power curve as the reference
+
+The bin-mean power curve is the industry's simplest performance model. Modelling the residual lets the network absorb wind-speed binning, air density and control mode explicitly rather than forcing the reader to attribute them.
+
+### Underperformance versus damage
+
+A residual can mean blade erosion, a dirty filter, icing or a curtailment instruction. The anomaly record is honest about being a performance signal; classification and XAI decide whether it is a fault.
+
+## Platform contract
 
