-## Structure
+Records follow the shared `WTDataSchema` (`wt-pm.platform.v1`): `timestamp`, `turbine_id` and `model_id` are required; every other field is optional, so a model fills in only what it honestly produces and the fusion layer can tell absence from a zero.
+
+## Platform layers
+
+| Layer | What this model does there |
+|---|---|
+| **Fusion** | Anomaly voter and the fallback target for m06's long-horizon forecasts |
+| **Hermes** | anomaly tool - power-curve residual is the first thing the agent checks on an underperformance question |
+| **RUL** | Power-curve degradation is an input feature for the RUL regressors |
+| **Fallback** | Receives falls back from m06 and falls back to m04 itself |
+
+Layers are described once, in the catalog, and referenced by every model that participates in them: fusion, calibrated uncertainty, drift and data trust, explainability, physics constraints, the safety gate, the evaluation protocol and the Hermes agent.
+
+## How it connects to the other 24
+
+**Receives from**
+
+- **11. Informer Long Sequence** (`m06-informer-forecast`) - long-horizon power forecast vs the actual curve
+
+**Feeds**
+
+- **14. MLP RUL Regression** (`m17-mlp-rul`) - power-curve degradation as a RUL feature
+
+Related pages: [11 Informer](https://github.com/rajaram-2005/wt-pm-informer-long-sequence), [14 MLP RUL](https://github.com/rajaram-2005/wt-pm-mlp-rul-regression)
+
