+<h1>TCN Power Curve</h1>
+<p class="lede">A causal temporal convolutional network that tracks the aerodynamic power curve and flags residual drift away from it. It is the collection's fastest way to answer the oldest question in wind O&amp;M: is this turbine producing what its own history says it should at this wind speed?</p>
+<div class="cta">
+<a class="btn" href="https://github.com/rajaram-2005/wt-pm-tcn-power-curve">View on GitHub</a>
+<a class="btn ghost" href="https://rajaram-2005.github.io/wt-pm-lstm-scada-anomaly/ecosystem.html">25-model ecosystem graph</a>
+<a class="btn ghost" href="https://github.com/rajaram-2005/wt-pm-lstm-scada-anomaly/blob/main/ARCHITECTURE.md">Platform architecture</a>
+</div>
+</header>
+<p class="note">This page is generated from <code>deployment/models.catalog.json</code> in the reference repository, together with the other 24 model pages, so all 25 agree on numbering, contract and status.</p>
+<h2>Model</h2>
+<ul>
+<li><code>TemporalConvNet in model.py</code></li>
+<li><code>Platform adapter trains it against the power channel</code></li>
+</ul>
+<table>
+<tr><th>Dilated causal convolutions</th><td>Kernel size k over L layers with exponentially growing dilation; the receptive field grows as (k-1) * 2^L</td></tr>
+<tr><th>Residual blocks</th><td>Each block adds its input back, which keeps deep stacks trainable</td></tr>
+<tr><th>Head</th><td>Power forecast for the next step; residual against measured power is the anomaly score</td></tr>
+</table>
+<h2>Advanced concepts</h2>
+<p class="note">The ideas this model actually leans on, each stated with its failure mode.</p>
+<div class="card">
+<h3>Receptive field by dilation</h3>
+<p>Two conv layers with kernel 3 see 5 samples; with dilation 1, 2, 4 the same two layers see 15. Causal TCNs buy long memory with convolution parallelism instead of recurrence's sequential dependency.</p>
+</div>
+<div class="card">
+<h3>Power curve as the reference</h3>
+<p>The bin-mean power curve is the industry's simplest performance model. Modelling the residual lets the network absorb wind-speed binning, air density and control mode explicitly rather than forcing the reader to attribute them.</p>
+</div>
+<div class="card">
+<h3>Underperformance versus damage</h3>
+<p>A residual can mean blade erosion, a dirty filter, icing or a curtailment instruction. The anomaly record is honest about being a performance signal; classification and XAI decide whether it is a fault.</p>
+</div>
+<h2>Platform contract</h2>
+<table>
+<tr><th>Input (adapter view)</th><td>windows + power_kw channel</td></tr>
+<tr><th>Output</th><td>anomaly_score + prediction (power forecast)</td></tr>
+<tr><th>Record format</th><td><code>wt-pm.platform.v1</code></td></tr>
+<tr><th>Typical latency</th><td>3000 ms</td></tr>
+<tr><th>Deployment targets</th><td>cloud, edge_gpu</td></tr>
+<tr><th>Requirements</th><td>torch</td></tr>
+<tr><th>Fallback</th><td>m04-gru-scada-telemetry</td></tr>
+<tr><th>Subsystem focus</th><td>rotor_blades, converter</td></tr>
+<tr><th>Hermes tool</th><td><code>anomaly</code></td></tr>
+</table>
+<p class="note">Records follow the shared <code>WTDataSchema</code> (<code>wt-pm.platform.v1</code>). Only <code>timestamp</code>, <code>turbine_id</code> and <code>model_id</code> are required; absence is distinguishable from a zero.</p>
+<h2>Platform layers</h2>
+<table>
+<tr><th>Fusion</th><td>Anomaly voter and the fallback target for m06's long-horizon forecasts</td></tr>
+<tr><th>Hermes</th><td>anomaly tool - power-curve residual is the first thing the agent checks on an underperformance question</td></tr>
+<tr><th>RUL</th><td>Power-curve degradation is an input feature for the RUL regressors</td></tr>
+<tr><th>Fallback</th><td>Receives falls back from m06 and falls back to m04 itself</td></tr>
+</table>
+<h2>How it connects to the other 24</h2>
+<ul class="edges">
+<li><b>11. Informer Long Sequence</b> <span class="note">(m06-informer-forecast)</span> &rarr; long-horizon power forecast vs the actual curve</li>
+<li>&rarr; <b>14. MLP RUL Regression</b> <span class="note">(m17-mlp-rul)</span> - power-curve degradation as a RUL feature</li>
+</ul>
+<h2>Honest limits</h2><ul class="limits">
+<li>A performance residual is not a fault label - curtailment and icing look identical statistically</li>
+<li>Causal convolutions trade receptive field for latency headroom on the edge</li>
+</ul>
+<p class="note">Fidelity: rung 1 of the fidelity ladder - simulator data, surrogate waveforms where stated, proxy RUL targets, simulator fault labels. Comparable within this collection, not field-validated turbine control.</p>
